WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.293
The easiest interpretation boundary to
secure is one the application never creates.

2
00:00:05.373 --> 00:00:08.568
If a profile name, status message, or
search term is text,

3
00:00:08.648 --> 00:00:13.308
assign it with textContent,
createTextNode, or normal framework interpolation.

4
00:00:13.388 --> 00:00:16.050
These APIs construct character data
directly.

5
00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:20.457
They do not ask the HTML parser to decide
whether the value contains elements,

6
00:00:20.537 --> 00:00:22.667
attributes, or executable behavior.

7
00:00:22.747 --> 00:00:24.944
Build structure with structural APIs.

8
00:00:25.024 --> 00:00:28.419
Create an element, attach known classes,
populate its text,

9
00:00:28.499 --> 00:00:30.230
and append it to a known parent.

10
00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:34.370
This keeps developer-authored structure
separate from external data.

11
00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:39.177
Concatenating strings into an HTML
fragment collapses those roles and forces every

12
00:00:39.257 --> 00:00:43.517
inserted value to be correct for its exact
location in the generated source.

13
00:00:43.597 --> 00:00:47.924
One missed or differently interpreted
insertion becomes a security defect.

14
00:00:48.004 --> 00:00:49.934
Safe is still property-specific.

15
00:00:50.014 --> 00:00:53.742
Assigning textContent on an ordinary
element has text semantics,

16
00:00:53.822 --> 00:00:55.619
but assigning href, src, style,

17
00:00:55.699 --> 00:00:59.494
or a script-related property invokes
different browser behavior.

18
00:00:59.574 --> 00:01:04.233
A link label can be rendered safely as
text while its destination still requires URL

19
00:01:04.313 --> 00:01:06.510
parsing and protocol or origin policy.

20
00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:08.853
Attribute names should be fixed by code.

21
00:01:08.933 --> 00:01:12.927
A property setter is not universally safe
merely because it is a DOM API.

22
00:01:13.007 --> 00:01:17.667
Treat innerHTML, outerHTML,
insertAdjacentHTML, document-writing functions,

23
00:01:17.747 --> 00:01:21.209
and string-based HTML parsing as
security-sensitive sinks.

24
00:01:21.289 --> 00:01:25.682
Framework raw-HTML features create the
same boundary under a different name.

25
00:01:25.762 --> 00:01:30.222
Use them only when the requirement is
genuinely to interpret HTML and a reviewed

26
00:01:30.302 --> 00:01:32.499
sanitization path supplies the value.

27
00:01:32.579 --> 00:01:36.906
For ordinary interfaces, state the
semantics directly: text uses text APIs,

28
00:01:36.986 --> 00:01:41.113
event behavior uses event listeners, URLs
use validated URL properties,

29
00:01:41.193 --> 00:01:44.321
and structure uses element or component
construction.

30
00:01:44.401 --> 00:01:49.194
Avoid converting data into source code
when the platform already offers a structured

31
00:01:49.274 --> 00:01:49.940
operation.
